## 4. Data Model

```mermaid
erDiagram
  INSTRUCTOR ||--o{ COURSE : teaches
  STUDENT ||--o{ ENROLLMENT : makes
  COURSE ||--o{ ENROLLMENT : has
  COURSE ||--o{ LESSON : contains
  LESSON ||--|{ SEGMENT : split_into
  LESSON ||--o{ LESSON_FORMAT : offers
  SEGMENT ||--o| CHECK_IN_QUESTION : ends_with
  STUDENT ||--o{ PROGRESS : records
  SEGMENT ||--o{ PROGRESS : tracked_in
  STUDENT ||--o{ ACHIEVEMENT : earns
  STUDENT ||--|| PREFERENCE : has
```

| Entity | Meaning |
|---|---|
| INSTRUCTOR, STUDENT | Account holders |
| COURSE | A course taught by one instructor |
| ENROLLMENT | Links a student to a course. It resolves the many-to-many between them. |
| LESSON | A video or PDF lesson in a course |
| SEGMENT | A short piece of a lesson (about 250 words), at least one per lesson |
| LESSON_FORMAT | Transcript, instructor-written text version, or visual summary of a lesson |
| CHECK_IN_QUESTION | The question at the end of a segment, with its options, answer, and explanation |
| PROGRESS | A student's result on a segment: completion, resume position, and check-in result |
| ACHIEVEMENT | Streaks and badges |
| PREFERENCE | One saved set of display and format settings per student |

### Cardinalities

| Entity A | Relationship | Entity B | A to B |
|---|---|---|---|
| INSTRUCTOR | teaches | COURSE | 1 to 0..N |
| STUDENT | makes | ENROLLMENT | 1 to 0..N |
| COURSE | has | ENROLLMENT | 1 to 0..N |
| COURSE | contains | LESSON | 1 to 0..N |
| LESSON | split into | SEGMENT | 1 to 1..N |
| LESSON | offers | LESSON_FORMAT | 1 to 0..N |
| SEGMENT | ends with | CHECK_IN_QUESTION | 1 to 0..1 |
| STUDENT | records | PROGRESS | 1 to 0..N |
| SEGMENT | tracked in | PROGRESS | 1 to 0..N |
| STUDENT | earns | ACHIEVEMENT | 1 to 0..N |
| STUDENT | has | PREFERENCE | 1 to 1 |

**Modeling notes**
- Each course has one instructor. Co-instructors would need an extra link entity.
- A check-in question stores its own answer options, so there is no separate options entity.
- Flashcards and expandable details are part of a segment's content.
- Points and the instructor drop-off counts are calculated from PROGRESS, so they need no entity of their own.
- Audio comes from the text version through text-to-speech at runtime, so it needs no entity.

