## 6. Key Workflow: Publishing a Lesson

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  A[Instructor uploads video or PDF] --> B[System suggests segments of about 250 words]
  B --> C[Instructor adjusts break points]
  C --> D[Instructor confirms segments]
  D --> E[Instructor writes check-in questions]
  E --> F{Video lesson: every segment has a question?}
  F -- No --> E
  F -- Yes --> G[Publish lesson]
  G --> H[Enrolled students study, answer, and resume]
```

## 7. Business Rules

| Area | Rule |
|---|---|
| Chunking | Suggestions target about 250 words (the default can be changed) and break only at sentence ends. A leftover shorter than 30% of the target joins the previous segment. |
| Chunking | Nothing is saved until the instructor confirms. Confirming again replaces the old segments and their questions. |
| Chunking | A published lesson cannot be re-segmented. |
| Estimated length | Video segments use real duration. Text uses 200 words per minute. |
| Publishing | A lesson needs confirmed segments. A video lesson also needs a check-in question on every segment. |
| Check-in question | One per segment, with 2 to 4 distinct options and a valid correct answer. |
| Check-in question | A video question cannot be deleted once the lesson is published. |
| Answering | The student must be enrolled and the lesson published. Options keep a fixed order, with no timer, score, or penalty, and the student can retry. |
| Enrollment | A student can enroll in a course only once. |
| Accounts | Passwords are at least 8 characters and are hashed with a salt. Emails are not case-sensitive. A failed login gives the same message for a wrong email or password. |

## 8. Accessibility Approach

Accessibility is a design rule for every screen, not a separate feature. The interface is designed to align with WCAG 2.1 Level AA.

- **Keyboard:** every action works without a mouse, with visible focus and a logical order.
- **Screen readers:** semantic HTML, labeled controls, and live announcements for check-in feedback and progress changes.
- **Visual:** sufficient contrast, adjustable text size and spacing, and no content that depends on color alone.
- **Motion and sound:** nothing flashes, and a low-stimulation mode turns off animation and sound effects.
- **Media:** captions on by default, a searchable transcript, and a text alternative for every video.
- **No time pressure:** no timers or countdowns anywhere.
- **Verification:** Lighthouse, axe, and a keyboard-only walkthrough, with results recorded in each pull request.

## 9. Security and Privacy

- Real secrets are never committed. `.env` is ignored, and `.env.example` holds placeholders only.
- Passwords are stored as PBKDF2 hashes with a random salt and compared in constant time.
- The student view of a question never includes the correct answer.
- Preferences and progress are private to the student. The instructor dashboard shows counts only and never identifies individuals.
- The system never asks about a diagnosis or disability.
- Sign-in and in-memory storage are course-project grade. A production version would use a dedicated authentication provider and a managed database.

