## 11. Design Decisions

| Decision | Reason |
|---|---|
| Standalone app alongside an LMS, not a plug-in | A true plug-in needs a specific LMS and its admin access, which is beyond the scope of the course |
| Semi-automatic chunking | The system suggests and the instructor confirms, which is reliable, keeps the instructor in control, and avoids needing AI |
| Instructor-supplied captions and text versions | Automatic captioning and summarizing are out of scope and need paid services |
| Services take a shared database object | Storage can change from in-memory to a real database without touching the rules |
| No diagnosis or disclosure anywhere | Many students never register for formal support, so features must work for everyone |
| Calm feedback with no scoring | Pressure and penalties work against focus and follow-through |

